// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_UrgentTask1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2939852479" "Razor"
// DetailString :
"P2656683042" "Razor is a ninja. He can cut people in half with his eyes and eat rocks."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2275460643" "Clockwork"
// DetailString :
"P4280575659" "These Clockwork are WAY more advanced than those on Primal Earth. Luckily they aren't too smart. Anti-Matter must have watched Terminator and thought better than to make them too smart."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P648968299" "Communication Grid"
// DetailString :
"P2519736057" "Apparently Anti-Matter has an orbital cannon pointed at the enclosure. If the slightest hint of trouble reaches his ears he can push a button and turn this place into a radioactive smear on the face of the planet. Cutting the communications grid will prevent that signal from getting sent to Anti-Matter, at least, sent by the Clockwork."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3676124990" "Listen up and listen well, {HeroName}. This situation is ripe for the plundering, but before we can take advantage of this chaos we need to restore just enough order to ensure we survive.<br><br>I'll explain later, just understand that I know what I'm talking about and we don't have a lot of time. Do as you are told now, and reap the benefits later.<br><br>First order of business is locating a primal named Razor. He escaped along with some of his cronies, but while the Clockwork rounded everyone else up, he's still missing. We had a deal and I want to make sure he isn't trying to double cross me."
// AcceptString :
"P4179219329" "Find Razor"
// SendOffString :
"P3215322608" "Also, just in case you were thinking of taking me out of the equation. Bad idea. Anti-Matter's got an orbital anti-proton cannon that will destroy this entire site if he gets word one of a problem down here. I'd hate for my automated message to get sent off because of your selfishness.<br><br>I have a feeling this is the beginning of a beautiful partnership."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_UrgentTask1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2909007622" "I know Razor is somewhere in the enclosure, have you found him yet?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P891472412" "{HeroName}?<br><br>Heh, never thought I'd meet you like this, always figured the role would be reversed after I got the drop on you.<br><br>Nevermind all that. I'm a goner,  devoured got me and Deadlock left me here to die, that damn traitor. Oh well, it's only a matter of time now...<br><br>What's that? Dr. Leta sent you to find me. Yeah, that sounds like her, she's keeping tabs on everything around here.<br><br>Listen, you've got to help her out, she isn't joking about Anti-Matter having an orbital cannon pointed at us and ready to blast us into glass at a moment's notice. Just help her keep this place sane for awhile and then you can concentrate on getting your piece of the pie.<br><br>Now go. Tell her I'm out of commission, she'll turn to you for help."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_UrgentTask1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3547527643" "Talk to Dr. Leta"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2946431576" "Help Dr. Leta, she's a survivor."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1593659439" "So, Razor is finished, huh? I guess that leaves you and me. Your lucky day.<br><br>Here's the situation. The Clockwork were intent on just capturing the escaped primals until I started installing contingency plans for their inevitable failures. Now it seems they've detected my tamperings with the enclosure computer systems and are seeking to shut me down. I've managed to keep them from locking me out of most of the key systems, so now they are trying to physically remove me.<br><br>I need you to take down some Clockwork and make them rethink their strategy. As long as they don't dare assault me directly, we're in good shape. If they take me down, well, we'll all be radioactive glass inside of five minutes."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_UrgentTask1_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2047281503" "Defeat Clockwork"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P233536441" "It won't take much to convince the Clockwork that you are a higher priority threat than I am. I know you are used to being hunted so it shouldn't be anything new for you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P3140107050" "Alert. Threat detected.<em t=2>{HeroName}. Terminate."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P770179204" "Very well done, {HeroName}. You could make a career smashing stuff... That was a joke.<br><br>Anyway, moving right along. While you've been keeping the Clockwork off of me I managed to determine five hard lined junction boxes that will provide access to the enclosure's entire communication grid. I want you to disable it.<br><br>Go to each of the junction boxes and insert these codes at each. Once they are deactivated the Clockwork will be incapable of sending a signal to Anti-Matter's orbital lab. That ability will remain safely in my hands as an insurance policy."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_UrgentTask1_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2536477446" "Deactivate the Communication Grid"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P686447457" "You must be eager to be remembered as a radioactive shadow baked into a wall. Get to those junction boxes and shut down the communication grid."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2295573156" "Alright, let's test to make sure everything is shut down properly and... Perfect!<br><br>I'm so easy to please."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P620603216" "See, {HeroName}, working with me isn't such a tough stretch for you, is it?<br><br>Good, now that we have the place under some managable form of order we can get down to business. This enclosure has netted me quite a valuable side business of selling devoured samples to interested third parties in Praetoria. If you were to help me get some live specimens, and keep this place from collapsing in the chaos, I could cut you in on the very lucritive profits.<br><br>What do you say?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_Task1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DrLetalReport1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2993473222" "Dr. Keppel's Report"
// DetailString :
"P950671963" "FU FU FU"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DevouredRootsSamples 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1553294755" "Devoured Roots Samples"
// DetailString :
"P1542296116" "You've managed to strip several pieces off of the devoured roots around the enclosure and place them in these test tubes. They thrash wildly against the glass, and for a moment you worry that they might break free.<br><br>You need to deliver these to Dr. Keppel."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DrKeppelReport1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3658525400" "Dr. Leta's Report"
// DetailString :
"P2645129153" "<3 <3 <3"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2759841668" "The devouring earth seeded the ground with seeds before workers began construction of this site. Now those seeds have started growing into writhing roots, possibly at the command of their kin outside of the enclosure shield. I need you to destroy some of those roots and gather some samples.<br><br>These test tubes would be a reliable way of storing them, especially since I don't have any idea what they are capable of. So better safe than dead."
// AcceptString :
"P1831329443" "Destroy devouring roots"
// SendOffString :
"P558170659" "Once you've gathered the samples take them and this report over to Dr. Keppel in Facility A. It's on the other side of the enclosure, so you'll likely have to fend off some clockwork on your way.<br><br>Dr. Keppel should have a report for you to bring to me. If our network was working it would make this all so much easier."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_Task1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2108989672" "Destroy Devouring Roots"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2250947418" "Have you gathered the appropriate samples of the Devouring Roots like I asked? You'll need to take them over to Dr. Keppel with that report I gave you. We must understand the threat they pose, if any, to the enclosure."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P137125250" "Subject detected.<em t=1>Infection probability 78.2%.<em t=2>Terminate."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1059772649" "You got the {ITEM_NAME}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_Task1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1169769450" "Deliver samples and report to Dr. Keppel"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3430942142" "Now that you have the Devouring Root samples I need you to deliver them to Dr. Keppel Don't forget to give him my report."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1203580631" "How can I help you?<br><br>Devoured roots samples? Wow, let me guess, this was one of Leta's ideas.<br><br>I had better take those off your hands incase there is a chance they get us all infected... What's that you have there? Let me see that report.<br><br>Hmmm... great use of my time. Here, take this report to Leta and tell her to keep the reports coming, her insight and testings are superb."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3140061855" "Thank you, {HeroName}. I'll read over Dr. Keppel's report in a moment. I swear, that man is nuts. He can't keep things serious for a minute.<br><br>Anyway, not important. I have another task for you."
// RandomFameString :
"P3958075051" "string"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Leta_V_Task2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3806206254" "I need you to deal with an imminent threat.<br><br>Several primals have escaped from one of the prison blocks and it appears that they are intent on accessing one of the computer banks that I shut down. If they get that computer running then the clockwork may be able to get a signal out to Anti-Matter. Get down there and stop the Primals and destroy that computer, we can't afford to risk letting them run rampant."
// AcceptString :
"P2884696027" "Destroy the computer"
// SendOffString :
"P585812427" "Superb. Get down there and stop those meddling fools before it's too late."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P687961464" "Destroy the Computer"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4068310250" "My sources indicate that those primals are still trying to hack into the computer system. I hope the encryption codes hold, but I'd rather you take care of them like we talked about."

